# Whitelist. Every Dockerfile builds from the repo root, so only what one of
# them COPYs may enter the build context. Everything else stays out: the git
# history, .env files, vendored checkouts, core dumps, node_modules.
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!.python-version
!package.json
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!src/uniffy
!src/proto/gen/python
!src/proto/gen/typescript
!src/ui
!docs/*.md
!docs/documentation
!.docker/dev
!.docker/media

# Inside the allowed trees
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.venv
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/dist
**/reports
**/.ruff_cache
**/.pytest_cache
**/*.log
src/uniffy/tests
